The clerk gives me the large shirt.
I say thanks.
This time I go straight to the fitting room.
Today there is no line there.
I enter a room and close the door.
I take off my yellow raincoat.
And then I try on the new green shirt.
I stand in front of the mirror.
This shirt is bigger than the first shirt.
It is a good fit for me.
It is not tight on the shoulders at all.
It is much more comfortable to wear than the old shirt.
I like this size very much.
I take off the new shirt and change.
I come outside with that shirt.
